To find the intersection point \(Q\), solve the system:
\[
\begin{cases}
3x - 4y = 1 \quad \text{(1)} \\
x - 2y = -11 \quad \text{(2)}
\end{cases}
\]
Multiply equation (2) by 2: \(2x - 4y = -22\). Subtract this from equation (1): \((3x - 4y) - (2x - 4y) = 1 - (-22)\) → \(x = 23\). Substitute into (2): \(23 - 2y = -11\) → \(-2y = -34\) → \(y = 17\). Thus, \(Q = (23, 17)\).

